@echo off
rem Primer -- local, machine-only overrides. TEMPLATE.
rem
rem HOW TO USE
rem   copy env.local.bat.example  ->  env.local.bat
rem   fill in the values below
rem   double-click the root launcher as usual
rem
rem   env.local.bat is gitignored, this template is not. The repo carries the
rem   recipe and never a key.
rem
rem WHY HERE AND NOT .env
rem   app/llm/客户端.py reads the key straight out of os.environ, and nothing
rem   loads a .env file into os.environ. PRIMER_LLM_KEY is also not a field of
rem   app/配置.py. So a key put in .env is ignored -- silently. This file is
rem   the supported way to set it.
rem
rem   Only the root launcher reads this file. Starting uvicorn yourself from a
rem   shell or an IDE run config does NOT -- set the variable in that one too.
rem
rem PRECEDENCE
rem   Anything set here beats the machine-wide environment: the launcher calls
rem   this file before it opens the two windows, and they inherit it. That is
rem   what makes this the per-project switch. DASHSCOPE_API_KEY is left alone.
rem
rem WHY THE LINE ENDINGS MATTER -- read this before saving over the file
rem   Measured 2026-10-04. cmd.exe reads a .bat byte by byte in the OEM code
rem   page (cp936 here). In a file with bare LF endings, a multi-byte character
rem   that mis-decodes desynchronises cmd's read offset -- it lands mid-line
rem   and runs the tail as a command. What that looked like when tested:
rem
rem     ASCII key + LF     -> key set        OK
rem     ASCII key + CRLF   -> key set        OK
rem     Chinese   + CRLF   -> key set        OK
rem     Chinese   + LF     -> key NOT set    SILENT
rem
rem   The last row is the dangerous one: no error, nothing in the log, set just
rem   never happened, and the app fell back to the OLD machine-wide
rem   DASHSCOPE_API_KEY without saying so. That is exactly the mix-up this file
rem   exists to prevent.
rem
rem   So Chinese comments are fine here, bare LF is not. The root launcher is
rem   ASCII-only for the neighbouring reason: it is an LF file.

rem --------------------------------------------------------------------------
rem THIS project's LLM key. It wins over DASHSCOPE_API_KEY, which stays as the
rem machine-wide fallback -- leave that one alone.
rem Get a key at bailian.console.aliyun.com
rem --------------------------------------------------------------------------
set PRIMER_LLM_KEY=sk-put-your-new-key-here

rem --------------------------------------------------------------------------
rem Optional. Uncomment only what you want to override; everything else keeps
rem its default. The two 话术生成 / 需求分解 variants work the same way and
rem fall back to these three.
rem --------------------------------------------------------------------------
rem set PRIMER_LLM_BASE_URL=https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
rem set PRIMER_LLM_MODEL=qwen-plus
